' S-611 (2026-10-17): the parameters of one class member are private to that member. Three methods with a parameter of the same name and
' different types (STRING, F64, I32) used to be rejected ("UXB_MIXED_STRING_NUMERIC", G-NESNE-16): the first parameter's type was used in all of them.
' WASM prints neither strings nor floats (explicit rejection), so five engines run this.
CLASS Say
    PUBLIC
    METHOD SetS(v AS STRING)
        PRINT v
    END METHOD
    METHOD SetF(v AS F64)
        PRINT v * 2.0
    END METHOD
    METHOD SetI(v AS I32)
        PRINT v + 1
    END METHOD
END CLASS
DIM s AS Say = NEW Say()
s.SetS("a")
s.SetF(1.5)
s.SetI(4)
